SUMMARY:Beyond the Block: From Black to Green
LOCATION:5107 N 22nd St Tampa \, FL 33610 United States
DESCRIPTION:An exciting in-person Tampa event brought to you by the Black 
 Innovation Leaders of Florida in partnership with the Urban Futures Festiv
 al. Technology should generate real prosperity\, not remain locked behind 
 confusing terminology. Black Innovation Leaders of Florida and the Pinella
 s Diaspora Arts Project present a special Tampa edition of Beyond the Bloc
 k in partnership with the Urban Futures Festival. Taking the code from the
  black box and turning it into wealth for your family and community. Join 
 us at The Skills Center to learn actionable strategies to convert technolo
 gy and digital culture into sustainable economic mobility. EVENT DETAILS D
 ate: Saturday\, November 7 Time: 10:00 AM to 2:00 PM Location: The Skills 
 Center\, 5107 N 22nd St\, Tampa\, FL 33610 Perks: Free admission\, free on
 -site parking\, complimentary brunch Audience: Adults seeking tech roles o
 r looking to integrate tech into business operations Emcee: Ebony Vaz AGEN
 DA 10:15 AM - 10:30 AM: Registration 10:30 AM - 10:45 AM: Refreshments 10:
 45 AM - 10:50 AM: Welcome with Ebony Vaz 10:50 AM - 11:45 AM: Turning Code
  to Cash with Rose Lejiste 11:50 AM - 12:00 PM: Break 12:00 PM - 12:40 PM:
  A Paid Role for Everyone in eSports with Derek Watford 12:40 PM - 12:55 P
 M: You Take the Stage and Share What Youre Building 12:55 PM - 1:00 PM: Br
 eak 1:00 PM - 1:40 PM: IT Roles for Tomorrow with Jordyn Short and Tiffiny
  B 1:40 PM - 1:45 PM: Upcoming Events 1:45 PM - 2:00 PM: Networking FEATUR
 ED SPEAKERS AND HOSTS Derek Watford: Co-Founder of High Point Gamer and Fo
 unding Architect of the Skills Lab at The Skills Center. He designs digita
 l media infrastructure that transforms gaming and digital culture into dir
 ect career pathways and financial growth. Rose Lejiste: Founding Board Mem
 ber of Black Innovation Leaders of Florida\, guiding professionals on conv
 erting digital tools into revenue stream assets. Jordyn Short Tiffiny B: T
 ech professionals leading practical discussions on securing emerging IT ca
 reer opportunities. Ebony Vaz: Founding Board Member of Black Innovation L
 eaders of Florida\, hosting and guiding the days discussions. HOSTED AND S
 PONSORED BY: Black Innovation Leaders of Florida Pinellas Diaspora Arts Pr
 oject Reserve your spot today! Dont let digital skills pass you by as tech
 nology expands. Secure your seat at no cost and start building your tech s
 trategy now. \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa.gov/node/197491
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/197491
END:VEVENT
