SUMMARY:Clay Aiken\, Andr DeShields Seth Rudetsky in Concert
LOCATION:1910 N. Ola Avenue Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:CAN Community Healths World AIDS Day Concert 2026  Tampa\, FL 
 - Presented by ViiV Healthcare Featuring Clay Aiken Special Opening Perfor
 mance by Andr De Shields Music Directed by Seth Rudetsky Join CAN Communit
 y Health for an extraordinary evening of music\, remembrance\, and communi
 ty as the Second Annual World AIDS Day Concert returns to Tampa. Held at T
 he Gathering at Armature Works\, this special concert brings together accl
 aimed artists\, advocates\, and our community to honor the lives affected 
 by HIV\, remember those we have lost to AIDS-related illnesses\, celebrate
  the extraordinary progress made over the past 35 years\, and renew our co
 mmitment to ending the HIV epidemic. Headlining the evening is acclaimed r
 ecording artist\, actor\, Broadway performer\, and advocate Clay Aiken\, b
 ringing his unmistakable voice and powerful stage presence to this meaning
 ful celebration. The evening will open with a special performance by legen
 dary Tony\, Grammy\, and Emmy Award winner Andr De Shields. One of America
 n theaters most celebrated performers\, De Shields brings decades of artis
 try\, storytelling\, and an extraordinary spirit to the World AIDS Day sta
 ge. Bringing it all together is Seth Rudetsky\, acclaimed Broadway musicia
 n\, actor\, author\, and SiriusXM Radio Broadway host\, who will serve as 
 the evenings Music Director. Presented during CAN Community Healths 35th a
 nniversary year\, the concert is more than a night of incredible entertain
 ment. It is an opportunity to come together as a communityto remember\, to
  celebrate\, and to recognize that the work continues. World AIDS Day is o
 bserved around the globe as a time to increase awareness about HIV\, chall
 enge stigma and discrimination\, encourage testing and prevention\, and af
 firm that people living with HIV deserve equitable access to compassionate
 \, high-quality care. Proceeds from the evening will benefit the Susan Ter
 ry Foundation\, continuing the legacy of CAN Community Health founder Susa
 n Terry by supporting organizations and initiatives that improve health\, 
 advance dignity\, and strengthen communities. Produced in partnership with
  Gray Box Theater and HarmonyWaves. Come experience an unforgettable eveni
 ng where music meets missionas Tampa gathers to remember those we have los
 t\, celebrate those living and thriving with HIV\, and look toward a futur
 e filled with hope\, dignity\, and the possibility of ending the HIV epide
 mic. Enhance your experience with Cocktails for a Cause presented by Shuma
 ker. Limited availability. Raise a glass to an unforgettable evening of co
 nnection\, entertainment\, and giving back. Cocktails for a Cause offers a
 n exclusive VIP experience featuring access to celebrated artists Clay Aik
 en\, Andr De Shields\, and Seth Rudetsky\, along with opportunities to min
 gle with fellow community leaders\, philanthropists\, and supporters. Enjo
 y an open bar and complimentary hors doeuvres\, then take your place in a 
 premium reserved seating section for the concert. \n\nPermalink: https://w
 ww.tampa.gov/node/197481
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/197481
END:VEVENT
